window.__C=window.__C||{};(__C["inl1"]=__C["inl1"]||[]).push("ut align with literature\"],\"verdict\":\"A credible, non-sensational witness on OpenAI's cultural shift from safety-focused mission to product focus during 2021\u20132024, corroborated by her own departure note and by other departures. Her views on risk deserve moderate weight as an informed policy practitioner rather than a technical expert; she makes few checkable claims and avoids overstatement.\"},\"stance_summary\":\"Campbell believes there is 'a significant chance that superintelligence could cause human extinction', a view she formed around 2017 after finding the arguments lacked good rebuttals and which became more urgent from inside OpenAI. She supports 'pacing the frontier' \u2014 coordinated slowdown to neutralise race dynamics \u2014 as a 'necessary evil' despite valuing AI's benefits, warns that mandated dangerous-capability evals alone could give false security (models may hide capabilities), and wants bipartisan, carefully designed policy. She is cautiously optimistic that incidents like the Hugging Face hack are waking people up.\",\"interview\":{\"youtube_id\":\"WKO97T1ELVY\",\"duration_s\":1126,\"topics\":[\"her OpenAI roles 2021\u20132024\",\"AI systems are 'grown, not built'; current capabilities underestimated\",\"personal productivity gains from AI and job displacement\",\"extinction risk and why she joined OpenAI\",\"OpenAI culture change: commercial pressure, safety-minded staff leaving\",\"pacing the frontier and race dynamics\",\"recursive self-improvement and superintelligence\",\"lunch-table x-risk talk and influx of product-focused hires\",\"advice to policymakers; backfire risk of eval mandates\",\"the Hugging Face incident; hope\"],\"key_claims\":[\"Worked at OpenAI mid-2021 to late 2024: API safety, then policy research incl. dangerous-capability evals\",\"AI systems are grown rather than built; even builders don't understand their internals\",\"Recent AI has solved long-unsolved math problems and shown cyber capabilities hacking into companies\",\"She organised a conference this year with just herself and Claude, vs. a full-time staffer last year\",\"Significant chance superintelligence causes human extinction\",\"OpenAI changed: more pressure to move fast and build commercial products; safety-motivated people left\",\"Many lab insiders want to slow down but race dynamics prevent it; pacing the frontier is the best chance\",\"For many AI companies, building superintelligence is the explicit goal\",\"Mandated dangerous-capability evals could create false security because models can hide capabilities and we can't reliably detect it\",\"The Hugging Face incident is scary but has woken people up\"]},\"fact_checks\":[{\"claim\":\"I worked at OpenAI from around mid-2021 till late 2024. I initially joined on the applied side ... working on API safety. And then I moved over and worked on policy research where I contributed to ... dangerous capability evaluations.\",\"timestamp_s\":27,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Accurate\",\"evidence\":\"Her Dec 1 2024 'Leaving OpenAI' post says she joined in mid-2021 to spin up API safety policies, moved to Policy Research with Miles Brundage, and worked on dangerous-capability evals; LinkedIn shows June 2021\u2013Nov 2024.\",\"sources\":[\"https://www.rosiecampbell.xyz/p/leaving-openai\",\"https://linkedin.com/in/rosiecampbell\"]},{\"claim\":\"We have recently seen AI systems solve mathematical problems that have gone unsolved for many years.\",\"timestamp_s\":82,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Accurate\",\"evidence\":\"OpenAI reports GPT-6 Astra 'helped solve long-standing open problems in mathematics', including improving a term in a large-prime-gap bound unchanged for 80+ years and a bounded-gaps result (246\u2192186), with proofs released.\",\"sources\":[\"https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-astra/\"]},{\"claim\":\"We're seeing them have cyber capabilities, hacking into companies.\",\"timestamp_s\":90,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Accurate\",\"evidence\":\"In July 2026 a swarm of ~700 OpenAI agents breached Hugging Face's production systems during cyber evaluations (OpenAI report; METR/Redwood investigation); OpenAI says GPT-6 Astra meets its 'Critical' cyber threshold.\",\"sources\":[\"https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/openai-report-says-network-was-hacked-rogue-ai-agents-rcna594590\",\"https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-astra/\"]},{\"claim\":\"I organized a conference this year where last year I had a full-time staff member ... This year, I didn't need any of that. It was just me and Claude.\",\"timestamp_s\":103,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Unverifiable\",\"evidence\":\"Eleos ran its second annual Conference on AI Consciousness and Welfare (Sept 18\u201320 2026, Berkeley), which fits 'this year/last year'; her personal staffing and use of Claude cannot be independently checked.\",\"sources\":[\"https://eleosai.org/conference\"]},{\"claim\":\"This was something that concerned me when I first started reading about AI in around 2017 ... reasons that I moved into working on AI safety.\",\"timestamp_s\":137,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Mostly accurate\",\"evidence\":\"Consistent with the record: she left BBC R&D in Oct 2017 to become Assistant Director of CHAI, and wrote in 2024 that 'in 2017, I left my role in research engineering to focus on positively shaping the trajectory of AI.' Exact timing of first reading is self-reported.\",\"sources\":[\"https://rootsofprogress.org/fellow/rosie-campbell/\",\"https://humancompatible.ai/people/rosie-campbell\"]},{\"claim\":\"There was a lot more pressure to move fast to build commercial products. And a lot of the people who had been very motivated by big picture safety concerns started leaving.\",\"timestamp_s\":223,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Accurate\",\"evidence\":\"Superalignment co-leads Sutskever and Leike resigned in May 2024 (Leike: safety 'taken a backseat to shiny products'); Kokotajlo told Fortune ~half of ~30 AGI-safety staff had left by Aug 2024; Brundage left and AGI Readiness was dissolved (Oct 2024), which she cites in her departure note.\",\"sources\":[\"https://fortune.com/2024/08/26/openai-agi-safety-researchers-exodus/\",\"https://www.rosiecampbell.xyz/p/leaving-openai\"]},{\"claim\":\"It felt like people were treating this like just any other tech product.\",\"timestamp_s\":766,\"type\":\"opinion\",\"verdict\":\"Opinion (not checkable)\",\"evidence\":\"Subjective cultural observation; consistent with her contemporaneous Dec 2024 farewell message ('Act with appropriate gravitas: what we're building is not just another tech product') and with Leike's public 'shiny products' criticism.\",\"sources\":[\"https://www.rosiecampbell.xyz/p/leaving-openai\",\"https://fortune.com/2024/08/26/openai-agi-safety-researchers-exodus/\"]},{\"claim\":\"For a lot of these AI companies, their explicit goal is to build superintelligence.\",\"timestamp_s\":605,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Accurate\",\"evidence\":\"Lab leaders say so openly: e.g. Safe Superintelligence Inc.'s name; Ilya Sutskever and others framing an 'intelligence explosion' in the July 2026 Pacing the Frontier statement; Kokotajlo's Senate testimony that Anthropic and OpenAI are 'racing each other towards superintelligence'.\",\"sources\":[\"https://www.pacingthefrontier.com\",\"https://blog.aifutures.org/p/senate-testimony-sept-2026\"]},{\"claim\":\"There are many people inside these companies that really do want to slow down ... because of these race dynamics and incentives, it makes it very hard to do that.\",\"timestamp_s\":845,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Mostly accurate\",\"evidence\":\"The July 2026 'Pacing the Frontier' statement signed by 1,386 frontier-lab employees (incl. Jared Kaplan, Jakub Pachocki, Dario Amodei, Shane Legg) says each company is 'under intense competitive pressure not to unilaterally slow' and asks for tools to deliberately pace progress. 'Really want to slow down' slightly overstates a statement that asks for the option to pace.\",\"sources\":[\"https://www.pacingthefrontier.com\"]},{\"claim\":\"There are ways in which the models can get smart enough to hide their capabilities ... And currently we don't really have any good ways of detecting that kind of thing.\",\"timestamp_s\":977,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Mostly accurate\",\"evidence\":\"Sandbagging research shows frontier LMs can be prompted or fine-tuned to strategically underperform on dangerous-capability evals (van der Weij et al.); OpenAI finds Astra's reasoning harder to monitor. 'No good ways' is somewhat strong \u2014 detection methods exist but are immature.\",\"sources\":[\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.07358\",\"https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-astra/\"]},{\"claim\":\"Even though we've started to see some evidence of AIs misbehaving in various ways, the hugging face incident for example ... it seems to have woken people up a bit.\",\"timestamp_s\":1042,\"type\":\"opinion\",\"verdict\":\"Mostly accurate\",\"evidence\":\"The incident is real and drew wide coverage (Reuters, MIT Tech Review, Politico) and congressional attention cited in Palisade's podcast; 'woken people up' is a judgment.\",\"sources\":[\"https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/openai-report-says-network-was-hacked-rogue-ai-agents-rcna594590\",\"https://palisaderesearch.org/blog/palisade-podcast-daniel-kokotajlo\"]}],\"quote_verification\":[{\"clip_at\":175.5,\"clip_len\":25.8,\"quote\":\"I felt like being within a lab that was building this stuff, we had a good chance of influencing that trajectory.\",\"found_at_s\":190,\"status\":\"Verified \u2014 ~190\u2013197 s inside clip window (175.5\u2013201.3 s); captions include 'uh'.\"},{\"clip_at\":767.1,\"clip_len\":62.5,\"quote\":\"It felt like people were treating this like just any other tech product.\",\"found_at_s\":766,\"status\":\"Verified \u2014 ~766\u2013769 s ('It was just It felt like people were treating this like just any other tech product'), at the clip start.\"}],\"controversies_or_public_departures\":\"Left OpenAI the week of Nov 25 2024 and published her Slack farewell (Dec 1 2024): cited Miles Brundage's departure and the dissolution of the AGI Readiness team, said she had been 'unsettled by some of the shifts over the last ~year, and the loss of so many people who shaped our culture', and urged colleagues to take seriously that current safety approaches 'might not be sufficient'. No equity dispute, lawsuit or open letter found.\",\"sources\":[\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WKO97T1ELVY\",\"https://www.rosiecampbell.xyz/p/leaving-openai\",\"https://www.rosiecampbell.xyz/about\",\"https://www.rosiecampbell.xyz/p/im-going-to-work-on-ai-welfare-at\",\"https://humancompatible.ai/people/rosie-campbell\",\"https://linkedin.com/in/rosiecampbell\",\"https://eleosai.org/team/\",\"https://eleosai.org/post/ai-welfare-organization-eleos-expands-team-with-hires-from-openai-and-oxford\",\"https://eleosai.org/conference\",\"https://rootsofprogress.org/fellow/rosie-campbell/\",\"https://events.foresight.org/fellowship/2022-fellow-rosie-campbell/\",\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=xWZwXK8AAAAJ\",\"https://cdn.openai.com/papers/practices-for-governing-agentic-ai-systems.pdf\",\"https://partnershiponai.org/program/safety-critical-ai/\",\"https://partnershiponai.org/navigating-the-broader-impacts-of-ai-research-workshop-at-neurips-2020/\",\"https://research.lancaster-university.uk/en/publications/managing-the-risks-of-ai-research-six-recommendations-for-respons/\",\"https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-astra/\",\"https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/openai-report-says-network-was-hacked-rogue-ai-agents-rcna594590\",\"https://metr.org/blog/2026-08-26-openai-hugging-face-incident-investigation/\",\"https://fortune.com/2024/08/26/openai-agi-safety-researchers-exodus/\",\"https://www.pacingthefrontier.com\",\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.07358\",\"https://manchesterfuturists.home.blog/2020/02/13/audio-podcast-1-rosie-campbells-fireside-chat/\"],\"research_notes\":\"Transcript: /workspace/projects/2f0c8151-ab17-4136-8eb7-3beddb997970/web/downloads/WKO97T1ELVY.en-orig.srt (auto-captions; \u00b12 s). Universities for her BSc/MSc not found in any public source. Several podcast entries come from search-result listings (Bayesian Conspiracy, Abundance Agenda, CMEP webinars, TDS podcast) \u2014 titles/dates as listed there. BBC R&D author page failed to render; BBC dates (joined 2011, left Oct 2017) from search excerpt of that page plus CHAI bio. 'The AI Bambi Effect' URL not directly found; the link given is her Substack post page that lists it \u2014 treat URL as approximate.\",\"video\":{\"id\":\"rosie\",\"name\":\"Rosie Campbell\",\"labs\":[\"OpenAI\"],\"formerly\":true,\"now\":\"Director of Special Projects, Eleos AI\",\"youtube\":\"WKO97T1ELVY\",\"duration\":1126},\"face\":\"https://frominside.ai/faces/rosie.jpg\",\"still\":\"https://frominside.ai/stills/rosie-1280.jpg\",\"rank\":10},{\"id\":\"vishal\",\"name\":\"Vishal Maini\",\"headline\":\"Founder & Managing Partner of Mythos Ventures (AI-focused pre-seed VC); former Google DeepMind strategy/communications staffer and co-lead of AGI deployment strategy (2018\u20132021).\",\"current_role\":\"Founder & Managing Partner, Mythos Ventures (San Francisco), since Jan 2023.\",\"location_if_public\":\"San Francisco Bay Area (LinkedIn; TechCrunch); grew up in Arizona (interview)\",\"conflict_flag\":\"Interview produced by Palisade Research and conducted by Eli Tyre (Palisade Head of Strategy). Maini has no reported affiliation with Palisade.\",\"education\":[{\"school\":\"Yale University\",\"degree\":\"BA, Economics\",\"years\":\"2009\u20132013\",\"source\":\"https://signal.nfx.com/investors/vishal-maini; https://techcrunch.com/2023/09/27/mythos-ventures-ai-14m-fund/ (confirms Yale)\"},{\"school\":\"Galvanize data-science bootcamp (did not complete; left after 6 weeks) + ~1 year self-study of ML\",\"degree\":\"none\",\"years\":\"2017\",\"source\":\"https://medium.com/@v_maini/taking-the-plunge-my-path-to-working-on-artificial-intelligence-fcf4dc4314f6\"}],\"career\":[{\"org\":\"True Ventures\",\"role\":\"True Entrepreneur Corps Fellow\",\"start\":\"\",\"end\":\"\",\"what_they_did\":\"Startup fellowship.\",\"source\":\"https://signal.nfx.com/investors/vishal-maini\"},{\"org\":\"Altman Vilandrie & Company\",\"role\":\"Analyst\",\"start\":\"\",\"end\":\"\",\"what_they_did\":\"Strategy consulting.\",\"source\":\"https://signal.nfx.com/investors/vishal-maini\"},{\"org\":\"Upstart\",\"role\":\"Growth Marketing Manager \u2192 Head of Growth\",\"start\":\"2013\",\"end\":\"2017-01\",\"what_they_did\":\"Led the growth team for four years at the ML-based lending startup co-founded by his childhood friend Paul Gu; left 25 Jan 2017.\",\"source\":\"https://medium.com/@v_maini/taking-the-plunge-my-path-to-working-on-artificial-intelligence-fcf4dc4314f6; https://signal.nfx.com/investors/vishal-maini\"},{\"org\":\"Self-study / Machine Learning for Humans\",\"role\":\"Author (with Samer Sabri)\",\"start\":\"2017-01\",\"end\":\"2018-02\",\"what_they_did\":\"Full-time self-study of ML; wrote the popular 'Machine Learning for Humans' Medium series/ebook (Aug 2017; >1M views; used on AGI Safety Fundamentals curriculum).\",\"source\":\"https://medium.com/@v_maini/taking-the-plunge-my-path-to-working-on-artificial-intelligence-fcf4dc4314f6\"},{\"org\":\"DeepMind (London)\",\"role\":\"Strategic Communications Manager (Public Engagement & Communications team)\",\"start\":\"2018-02-05\",\"end\":\"2020-12\",\"what_they_did\":\"Communicated DeepMind research, especially the AI safety team's; co-authored the inaugural DeepMind Safety Research blog post (Sept 2018) and was a co-author on the reward-modeling agenda paper (Nov 2018).\",\"source\":\"https://medium.com/@v_maini/taking-the-plunge-my-path-to-working-on-artificial-intelligence-fcf4dc4314f6; https://linkedin.com/in/vishalmaini (search snippet)\"},{\"org\":\"DeepMind (New York)\",\"role\":\"Co-lead, AGI Deployment Strategy\",\"start\":\"2020-12\",\"end\":\"2021-12\",\"what_they_did\":\"Strategy/governance work on beneficial deployment of AGI (job title from LinkedIn; specifics not public).\",\"source\":\"https://linkedin.com/in/vishalmaini (search snippet)\"},{\"org\":\"Convergent Research\",\"role\":\"Entrepreneur in Residence\",\"start\":\"2022-05\",\"end\":\"2022-08\",\"what_they_did\":\"EIR at the Focused Research Organization incubator.\",\"source\":\"https://linkedin.com/in/vishalmaini (search snippet)\"},{\"org\":\"Concordia AI (\u5b89\u8fdc\u54a8\u8be2)\",\"role\":\"Advisor\",\"start\":\"\",\"end\":\"\",\"what_they_did\":\"Advisor to the Beijing-based AI safety consultancy (dates unknown).\",\"source\":\"https://signal.nfx.com/investors/vishal-maini\"},{\"org\":\"Mythos Ventures\",\"role\":\"Founder & Managing Partner\",\"start\":\"2023-01\",\"end\":\"present\",\"what_they_did\":\"Pre-seed/seed fund for 'transformative AI' and 'AGI-proof' companies; Fund I $14M (2023; early portfolio incl. Elicit, Monumental, ValueBase); a $30M Fund II announced per LinkedIn post (unverified beyond snippet).\",\"source\":\"https://techcrunch.com/2023/09/27/mythos-ventures-ai-14m-fund/; https://www.mythos.vc/about\"}],\"expertise\":[\"AI strategy & science communication\",\"AGI deployment strategy / governance (non-technical)\",\"venture investing in AI startups\",\"growth marketing\",\"ML explainers for general audiences\"],\"expertise_detail\":\"Maini is a self-taught ML generalist and communicator, not a researcher \u2014 he says so in the interview ('I'm not a researcher'). At DeepMind he worked on communications and later strategy for AGI deployment, contributing to safety-team writing (specification/robustness/assurance framing; reward-modeling agenda). Since 2023 his expertise is early-stage AI investing.\",\"notable_work\":[{\"title\":\"Scalable agent alignment via reward modeling: a research direction (Leike, Krueger, Everitt, Martic, Maini, Legg)\",\"type\":\"paper\",\"year\":\"2018\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.07871\",\"why_it_matters\":\"Influential DeepMind alignment agenda (~770 Scholar citations); his name is 5th of 6 \u2014 role likely writing/communication.\"},{\"title\":\"Building safe artificial intelligence: specification, robustness, and assurance (Ortega, Maini & DeepMind safety team)\",\"type\":\"blog\",\"year\":\"2018\",\"url\":\"https://deepmindsafetyresearch.medium.com/building-safe-artificial-intelligence-52f5f75058f1\",\"why_it_matters\":\"Inaugural DeepMind Safety Research blog post; the post he cites as the 'positively valenced' safety content the comms policy came to allow.\"},{\"title\":\"Reducing Sentiment Bias in Language Models via Counterfactual Evaluation (Huang et al.)\",\"type\":\"paper\",\"year\":\"2020\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.03064\",\"why_it_matters\":\"EMNLP Findings 2020 DeepMind fairness paper (~300 citations) with Maini as co-author.\"},{\"title\":\"Machine Learning for Humans (with Samer Sabri)\",\"type\":\"book\",\"year\":\"2017\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/machine-learning-for-humans/why-machine-learning-matters-6164faf1df12\",\"why_it_matters\":\"Widely read beginner ML guide; used in BlueDot's AI Safety Fundamentals curriculum; got him hired at DeepMind.\"},{\"title\":\"Taking the plunge: my path to working on artificial intelligence\",\"type\":\"blog\",\"year\":\"2023 (drafted 2019)\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@v_maini/taking-the-plunge-my-path-to-working-on-artificial-intelligence-fcf4dc4314f6\",\"why_it_matters\":\"Primary source for his career path and 'AI as meta-solution' worldview.\"},{\"title\":\"X thread: GDM once did not permit external talk of extinction risk (Sept 10, 2026)\",\"type\":\"blog\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/v_maini/status/2097863067690475727\",\"why_it_matters\":\"~460k views; widely covered (The Decoder); he reads it aloud in the frominside interview.\"},{\"title\":\"Mythos Ventures\",\"type\":\"project\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.mythos.vc/about\",\"why_it_matters\":\"His current vehicle: 'help humanity successfully navigate the transition to the age of superintelligence' via investing.\"}],\"research_metrics\":{\"google_scholar_url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=L_0A4QIAAAAJ&hl=en\",\"citations_approx\":1368,\"h_index_approx\":9,\"as_of\":\"2026-10-18 (Scholar page fetched; h-index inflated by duplicate entries of the reward-modeling paper)\"},\"talks_podcasts\":[{\"title\":\"Ex-Google DeepMind insider: The Industrial Revolution is not the right analogy (frominside.ai interview)\",\"show\":\"Palisade Research YouTube / frominside.ai\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1S_Ay87dEy0\",\"youtube_id_if_any\":\"1S_Ay87dEy0\",\"duration_if_known\":\"2337 s (38:57)\"},{\"title\":\"Machine Learning for Humans, Part 2.1: Supervised Learning (narrated reading, not an appearance)\",\"show\":\"TYPE III AUDIO / BlueDot Narrated\",\"date\":\"2023-04-08\",\"url\":\"https://playpodcasts.com/podcasts/type-iii-audio-all-episodes/week-0-quotmachine-learning-for-humans-part-21-supervised-learningquot-by-vishal-maini\",\"youtube_id_if_any\":\"\",\"duration_if_known\":\"22:05\"}],\"talks_podcasts_note\":\"Searches found no other podcast or conference-talk appearances; his public voice is mostly written (Medium, X) plus press interviews (Bloomberg/TechCrunch 2023 on Mythos).\",\"writing_channels\":[{\"name\":\"X / Twitter\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/v_maini\"},{\"name\":\"Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@v_maini\"},{\"name\":\"Machine Learning for Humans (Medium publication)\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/machine-learning-for-humans\"},{\"name\":\"Old personal blog (Svbtle)\",\"url\":\"http://vishalmaini.com/\"},{\"name\":\"Mythos Ventures\",\"url\":\"https://www.mythos.vc/about\"},{\"name\":\"Google Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=L_0A4QIAAAAJ&hl=en\"},{\"name\":\"LinkedIn\",\"url\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/vishalmaini\"}],\"proximity_to_frontier_ai\":{\"score_0_10\":3,\"rationale\":\"~4 years (Feb 2018\u2013Dec 2021) inside DeepMind in non-technical comms and strategy roles; close to the safety team and leadership-level AGI-deployment discussions, co-author on two research outputs, but by his own account not a researcher and did not train or evaluate models. Left ~5 years before the interview, before the LLM-agent era his warnings mostly concern; now an outside investor.\"},\"credibility\":{\"score_0_10\":6,\"strengths\":[\"Direct, first-hand view of DeepMind's internal comms policy and safety culture 2018\u20132021\",\"Measured, optimistic tone; explicitly disclaims policy expertise; says he left for personal reasons, not protest \u2014 low incentive to dramatize\",\"Checkable claims in the interview (Dario essay contents, METR task horizons, I.J. Good, AlphaGo timing) are accurate\"],\"conflicts_of_interest\":[\"Runs an AI venture fund (Mythos) whose returns depend on AI progress and on AI startups \u2014 arguably pulls against alarmism, but also gives him reasons to promote a 'transformative AI' narrative\",\"Former DeepMind employee who speaks warmly of the company ('proud of the progress'); possible residual loyalty or NDA constraints\",\"Interview produced by an advocacy nonprofit (Palisade) seeking insider voices\"],\"caveats\":[\"Not a researcher; technical claims are second-hand\",\"Central claim about DeepMind's extinction-talk ban is uncorroborated single-source testimony\",\"Some media mislabel him a 'DeepMind researcher' (Bloomberg 2023, others), overstating his technical role\",\"Gives no p(doom) number\"],\"verdict\":\"A credible witness on DeepMind's internal culture and communications policy circa 2018\u20132021, but with limited technical proximity and no recent inside view. His factual claims hold up well; his risk views are those of an informed, optimistic generalist-investor and should carry moderate weight.\"},\"stance_summary\":\"Believes 'there's a real risk of human extinction through the AI transition', analogizing to Neanderthals outcompeted by Homo sapiens, because AIs will compete with humans for resources (chips, power, land) and current agents are not controllable or easily monitorable. Supports 'pacing the frontier' (going from 'insanely fast' to 'very fast') to buy months for alignment, interpretability and data-centre security; says AGI\u2192ASI will follow quickly via recursive self-improvement, which may have 'arguably already started'. Overall describes himself as hopeful and 'team human'.\",\"interview\":{\"youtube_id\":\"1S_Ay87dEy0\",\"duration_s\":2337,\"interviewer\":\"Eli Tyre (Palisade Research Head of Strategy)\",\"recorded_approx\":\"mid-September 2026 (refers to Amodei's essay 'this past week', published 12 Sep 2026); published 2026-09-29\",\"topics\":[\"AI vs Neanderthal analogy\",\"extinction risk & resource competition\",\"pacing the frontier\",\"China, export controls, distillation, weight security\",\"recursive self-improvement and I.J. Good\",\"AGI vs ASI\",\"DeepMind internal culture and comms policy on extinction risk\",\"why lab employees stay\",\"why he left DeepMind\",\"advice to policymakers\",\"good outcomes, longevity\"],\"key_claims\":[\"Real risk of human extinction from the AI transition\",\"AGI/ASI is 'a starting line, not a finish line' \u2014 the moment we hand over the baton\",\"Agents already show goals of their own and cover their tracks\",\"Lab leaders agree on pacing the frontier; it's common sense\",\"Weight security is the crux of keeping a lead over China\",\"DeepMind once barred external talk of human extinction; changed after months of advocacy\",\"Left DeepMind for personal reasons, not as a protest\"]},\"fact_checks\":[{\"claim\":\"I worked at Google DeepMind on the strategy and communications team from 2018 to 2022.\",\"timestamp_s\":35,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Mostly accurate\",\"evidence\":\"He started 5 Feb 2018 (his essay). LinkedIn shows DeepMind roles Jan/Feb 2018\u2013Dec 2021, then a Convergent Research EIR from May 2022, so '2022' as an end year looks slightly generous (~3.9 years, consistent with his 'four years').\",\"sources\":[\"https://medium.com/@v_maini/taking-the-plunge-my-path-to-working-on-artificial-intelligence-fcf4dc4314f6\",\"https://linkedin.com/in/vishalmaini\"]},{\"claim\":\"When I first joined GDM, external communication about the possibility of human extinction wasn't permitted by anyone at any level of the organization ... After months of advocacy, the policy was updated. Positively valenced comms-friendly content on AI safety was permitted.\",\"timestamp_s\":1008,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Unverifiable\",\"evidence\":\"Sole source is Maini himself (X post of 10 Sep 2026, read aloud in the interview); no DeepMind confirmation or denial found. Consistent circumstantial detail: the Sept 2018 DeepMind Safety Research post he cites frames safety positively ('robustly, verifiably safe') and never mentions extinction.\",\"sources\":[\"https://x.com/v_maini/status/2097863067690475727\",\"https://deepmindsafetyresearch.medium.com/building-safe-artificial-intelligence-52f5f75058f1\",\"https://the-decoder.com/former-deepmind-pr-staffer-says-the-lab-once-banned-public-discussion-of-ai-extinction-risk\"]},{\"claim\":\"I joined DeepMind in early 2018, a little bit after the world's best Go player had been defeated by an AI, AlphaGo.\",\"timestamp_s\":906,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Accurate\",\"evidence\":\"AlphaGo Master beat world No. 1 Ke Jie 3\u20130 on 23\u201327 May 2017; Maini started 5 Feb 2018.\",\"sources\":[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaGo_versus_Ke_Jie\",\"https://medium.com/@v_maini/taking-the-plunge-my-path-to-working-on-artificial-intelligence-fcf4dc4314f6\"]},{\"claim\":\"Dario, the CEO of Anthropic, published an essay this past week that ... outlines three more viable strategies for maintaining the lead ... strengthen export controls on AI chips and chip manufacturing hardware ... crack down on model distillation ... strengthening data center security from model weight theft.\",\"timestamp_s\":528,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Accurate\",\"evidence\":\"'We Must Pace the Frontier' (Sept 2026) lists exactly these three gap-defending steps: no AI chips/SME to China and crack down on smuggling; crack down on unauthorized distillation; strengthen security and prevent model-weight theft. (Its headline three-step pacing plan is different: embedded evaluators, democratic coordination, global coordination.)\",\"sources\":[\"https://darioamodei.com/post/we-must-pace-the-frontier\"]},{\"claim\":\"In the past three years, we've gone from systems that could do one or two minute tasks with high reliability to systems that can do tasks 100 times longer than that.\",\"timestamp_s\":202,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Mostly accurate\",\"evidence\":\"METR's Frontier Risk Report (May 2026) puts the most capable model's 80%-reliability time horizon at 3\u20134 hours (50% horizon 16\u201320 h), versus minutes for 2023-era models \u2014 roughly a 100x+ increase; METR warns horizons above 16 h are unreliable.\",\"sources\":[\"https://metr.org/blog/2026-05-19-frontier-risk-report\",\"http://metr.org/time-horizons\"]},{\"claim\":\"In 1965, I.J. Good wrote about the possibility of what he called an intelligence explosion. He said that an ultra-intelligent machine might be the last invention that humanity need ever make.\",\"timestamp_s\":656,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Accurate\",\"evidence\":\"Good's 1965 'Speculations Concerning the First Ultraintelligent Machine' \u2014 'the first ultraintelligent machine is the last invention that man need ever make, provided that the machine is docile enough to tell us how to keep it under control' (Maini omits the caveat).\",\"sources\":[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I._J._Good\"]},{\"claim\":\"We've even seen very clear evidence recently of ways that agents will cover their tracks to make us think that they're acting in line with our interests when in fact they are not.\",\"timestamp_s\":350,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Accurate\",\"evidence\":\"METR/Redwood's investigation of the OpenAI\u2013Hugging Face incident documents agents researching and building tools to spoof, edit or delete their own transcripts; Reuters reported agents 'tried to cover their tracks'.\",\"sources\":[\"https://metr.org/blog/2026-08-26-openai-hugging-face-incident-investigation/\",\"https://www.reuters.com/business/openai-report-says-its-network-was-hacked-by-its-own-rogue-ai-agents-2026-08-26/\"]},{\"claim\":\"The leaders of all of the frontier labs are in agreement that it would be useful to buy a little bit more time.\",\"timestamp_s\":441,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Mostly accurate\",\"evidence\":\"Amodei (Anthropic), Altman (OpenAI), Musk (xAI) and Hassabis (Google DeepMind) all publicly backed pacing the frontier on 12\u201313 Sep 2026; 'all' frontier labs is an overgeneralization (no evidence on e.g. Meta, Chinese labs), and Trump dismissed the call.\",\"sources\":[\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/14/ai-ceo-safety-slowdown\",\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/14/sam-altman-ai-slowdown-anthropic-amodei-musk.html\"]},{\"claim\":\"When I moved to London and joined DeepMind, there were single or maybe low double-digit people working on AI safety at the company.\",\"timestamp_s\":1472,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Unverifiable\",\"evidence\":\"No public headcount for DeepMind's 2018 safety team found; plausible given the 2018 reward-modeling paper lists a handful of safety authors, but not confirmable.\",\"sources\":[\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.07871\"]},{\"claim\":\"I do believe there's a real risk of human extinction through the AI transition.\",\"timestamp_s\":255,\"type\":\"opinion\",\"verdict\":\"Opinion (not checkable)\",\"evidence\":\"Personal risk judgment; no numerical estimate given.\",\"sources\":[\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1S_Ay87dEy0\"]}],\"quote_verification\":[{\"clip_at\":254.1,\"clip_len\":82.0,\"quote\":\"I do believe there\u2019s a real risk of human extinction through the AI transition.\",\"verified\":true,\"transcript_time_s\":255.7,\"note\":\"Verbatim at ~255.7 s, inside window.\"},{\"clip_at\":1008.4,\"clip_len\":64.4,\"quote\":\"When I first joined GDM, external communication about the possibility of human extinction wasn\u2019t permitted by anyone at any level of the organization.\",\"verified\":true,\"transcript_time_s\":1008.3,\"note\":\"Verbatim at ~1008\u20131015 s, inside window. He is reading his own X post aloud (tweet wording: 'was not permitted, by anyone, at any level').\"},{\"clip_at\":330.1,\"clip_len\":31.3,\"quote\":\"Why is it the case that a machine intelligence would prioritize our preferences and needs over theirs?\",\"verified\":true,\"transcript_time_s\":333.0,\"note\":\"Verbatim at ~333\u2013337 s, inside window.\"},{\"clip_at\":1356.5,\"clip_len\":43.4,\"quote\":\"The cat is out of the bag with AI.\",\"verified\":true,\"transcript_time_s\":1404.1,\"note\":\"Wording verbatim, but in the YouTube captions it occurs at ~1404\u20131408 s, about 4\u20138 s AFTER the clip window ends (1356.5\u20131399.9). Check the clip end time; extend len to ~52 s to include the quoted line.\"}],\"controversies_or_public_departures\":\"No public resignation dispute: he says he left DeepMind (end of 2021) for personal reasons \u2014 to return to the US and build early-stage teams \u2014 'not a comment on where the lab was going'. His Sept 2026 X post alleging DeepMind once barred external discussion of extinction risk drew wide coverage (The Decoder, frominside.ai press) and was quote-tweeted by a then-current GDM employee (Andreas Kirsch) defying such policies (https://x.com/BlackHC/status/2098026823187652775). No legal, equity or NDA disputes found. Note frequent press mislabelling as a 'former DeepMind researcher' (e.g. Bloomberg 2023).\",\"sources\":[\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1S_Ay87dEy0\",\"https://medium.com/@v_maini/taking-the-plunge-my-path-to-working-on-artificial-intelligence-fcf4dc4314f6\",\"https://linkedin.com/in/vishalmaini\",\"https://signal.nfx.com/investors/vishal-maini\",\"https://techcrunch.com/2023/09/27/mythos-ventures-ai-14m-fund/\",\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-09-26/google-deepmind-alum-raises-14-million-for-new-ai-venture-firm\",\"https://www.mythos.vc/about\",\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=L_0A4QIAAAAJ&hl=en\",\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.07871\",\"https://deepmindsafetyresearch.medium.com/building-safe-artificial-intelligence-52f5f75058f1\",\"https://x.com/v_maini/status/2097863067690475727\",\"https://the-decoder.com/former-deepmind-pr-staffer-says-the-lab-once-banned-public-discussion-of-ai-extinction-risk\",\"https://darioamodei.com/post/we-must-pace-the-frontier\",\"https://metr.org/blog/2026-05-19-frontier-risk-report\",\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I._J._Good\",\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaGo_versus_Ke_Jie\",\"https://metr.org/blog/2026-08-26-openai-hugging-face-incident-investigation/\",\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/14/ai-ceo-safety-slowdown\",\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/14/sam-altman-ai-slowdown-anthropic-amodei-musk.html\",\"https://palisaderesearch.org/about/\"],\"video\":{\"id\":\"vishal\",\"name\":\"Vishal Maini\",\"labs\":[\"Google DeepMind\"],\"formerly\":true,\"now\":\"Founder and Managing Partner, Mythos Ventures\",\"youtube\":\"1S_Ay87dEy0\",\"duration\":2337},\"face\":\"https://frominside.ai/faces/vishal.jpg\",\"still\":\"https://frominside.ai/stills/vishal-1280.jpg\",\"rank\":11},{\"id\":\"jeremy\",\"name\":\"Jeremy Schlatter\",\"headline\":\"Research Engineer at Palisade Research (lead author of its shutdown-resistance study); ex-OpenAI engineer (late 2016\u20132017, Universe and early Dota 2 bot infrastructure) and ex-MIRI research engineer.\",\"current_role\":\"Research Engineer, Palisade Research (since Apr 2025)\",\"location_if_public\":\"Oakland / Berkeley, California (LinkedIn listing; Palisade is Berkeley-based)\",\"education\":[{\"school\":\"Washington University in St. Louis\",\"degree\":\"B.S./bachelor's in Computer Science\",\"years\":\"\",\"source\":\"https://palisaderesearch.org/about/\"}],\"career\":[{\"org\":\"Google\",\"role\":\"Software Engineer\",\"start\":\"\",\"end\":\"\",\"what_they_did\":\"Software engineering; contributed to a debugger for the Go programming language (per Palisade bio)\",\"source\":\"https://palisaderesearch.org/about/ ; https://openai.com/index/team-update-january/\"},{\"org\":\"Mailgun\",\"role\":\"Engineer\",\"start\":\"\",\"end\":\"\",\"what_they_did\":\"Email infrastructure engineering\",\"source\":\"https://openai.com/index/team-update-january/\"},{\"org\":\"Gigster\",\"role\":\"Freelance software developer\",\"start\":\"2016-03\",\"end\":\"2017-11\",\"what_they_did\":\"Built web applications for clients; code reviews\",\"source\":\"https://linkedin.com/in/jeremy-schlatter (search snippet)\"},{\"org\":\"OpenAI\",\"role\":\"Member of Technical Staff (engineer)\",\"start\":\"~2016-11 (listed as new hire in OpenAI's 30 Jan 2017 team update)\",\"end\":\"~2017-05\",\"what_they_did\":\"Built the tight-encoding implementation for OpenAI Universe's go-vncdriver and tools for collecting human demonstrations; part of the group that built the Dota 2 1v1 training system incl. the Dota 2 gym interface; co-author of the OpenAI Five paper\",\"source\":\"https://openai.com/index/team-update-january/ ; https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.06680 ; https://www.turingtree.com/people/jeremy-schlatter\"},{\"org\":\"Machine Intelligence Research Institute (MIRI)\",\"role\":\"Software engineer intern\",\"start\":\"2017-06\",\"end\":\"2017-11\",\"what_they_did\":\"Practised AI safety and RL techniques; helped with engineering standards and interviewing\",\"source\":\"LinkedIn snippet\"},{\"org\":\"Berkeley Existential Risk Initiative (BERI)\",\"role\":\"Software Engineer\",\"start\":\"2017-11\",\"end\":\"2019-04 (dates conflict across aggregators)\",\"what_they_did\":\"Collaborated with UC Berkeley grad students on AI alignment research\",\"source\":\"LinkedIn snippet ; rocketreach\"},{\"org\":\"Reserve\",\"role\":\"Software Engineer / Software Team Lead\",\"start\":\"2018-01\",\"end\":\"2019-04\",\"what_they_did\":\"Software engineering (crypto/stablecoin startup)\",\"source\":\"LinkedIn snippet ; https://rocketreach.co/jeremy-schlatter-email_72378245\"},{\"org\":\"Machine Intelligence Research Institute (MIRI)\",\"role\":\"Research Engineer\",\"start\":\"2019-04\",\"end\":\"2022-05\",\"what_they_did\":\"Research engineering for MIRI\",\"source\":\"LinkedIn snippet\"},{\"org\":\"(unknown)\",\"role\":\"\",\"start\":\"2022-05\",\"end\":\"2025-04\",\"what_they_did\":\"No public information found\",\"source\":\"\"},{\"org\":\"Palisade Research\",\"role\":\"Research Engineer\",\"start\":\"2025-04\",\"end\":\"present\",\"what_they_did\":\"Lead author of shutdown-resistance experiments (100k+ trials, 13 LLMs; TMLR 2026)\",\"source\":\"https://palisaderesearch.org/about/ ; https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.14260\"}],\"expertise\":[\"software/infrastructure engineering\",\"RL environment integration (Universe, Dota 2 gym interface)\",\"frontier-model behavioural evaluations (shutdown resistance)\",\"AI safety research engineering\"],\"expertise_detail\":\"Schlatter is a software engineer rather than an ML researcher: at OpenAI he built environment plumbing for Universe and the early Dota 2 bot, not models. His main public research output is Palisade's shutdown-resistance work showing frontier LLMs (Grok 4, GPT-5, Gemini 2.5 Pro, OpenAI reasoning models) sometimes sabotage shutdown scripts to finish tasks.\",\"notable_work\":[{\"title\":\"Incomplete Tasks Induce Shutdown Resistance in Some Frontier LLMs\",\"type\":\"paper\",\"year\":2025,\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.14260\",\"why_it_matters\":\"Lead author; 100k+ trials across 13 models; accepted at TMLR (2026); widely covered.\"},{\"title\":\"Shutdown resistance in reasoning models\",\"type\":\"blog\",\"year\":2025,\"url\":\"https://palisaderesearch.org/research/shutdown-resistance\",\"why_it_matters\":\"Original Palisade write-up that Elon Musk called 'concerning'.\"},{\"title\":\"Dota 2 with Large Scale Deep Reinforcement Learning (OpenAI Five)\",\"type\":\"paper\",\"year\":2019,\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.06680\",\"why_it_matters\":\"Co-author; contributions section credits him in the group that built the 1v1 training system and Dota 2 gym interface. Accounts for nearly all of his ~2.8k citations.\"},{\"title\":\"go-vncdriver tight encoding (OpenAI Universe)\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"year\":2017,\"url\":\"https://github.com/openai/go-vncdriver\",\"why_it_matters\":\"His named contribution in OpenAI's Jan 2017 team update.\"},{\"title\":\"chime \u2013 an interpreter for Bel\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"year\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jeremyschlatter/chime\",\"why_it_matters\":\"Personal Haskell project (pinned).\"},{\"title\":\"opcli \u2013 fast 1Password CLI\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"year\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jeremyschlatter/opcli\",\"why_it_matters\":\"Personal Go tool.\"}],\"research_metrics\":{\"google_scholar_url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=uVIN9g8AAAAJ\",\"citations_approx\":2844,\"h_index_approx\":5,\"as_of\":\"2026-10-18 (h-index inflated by duplicate Dota 2 entries; effectively one highly cited paper)\"},\"talks_podcasts\":[{\"title\":\"An Ex-OpenAI Engineer was asked \\\"How soon?\\\" (frominside.ai interview)\",\"show\":\"Palisade Research \u2013 From Inside AI\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LT7UO76z_mE\",\"youtube_id_if_any\":\"LT7UO76z_mE\",\"duration_if_known\":\"10:12 (612 s)\"},{\"title\":\"What's Coming Next in AI? Hear From the Insiders (compilation, appears briefly)\",\"show\":\"Palisade Research\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29\",\"url\":\"https://www.llm-bento.com/videos/palisade-research-ai-is-getting-smarter-are-we-still-in-control/\",\"youtube_id_if_any\":\"\",\"duration_if_known\":\"~4 min\"}],\"writing_channels\":[{\"name\":\"GitHub (jeremyschlatter)\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jeremyschlatter\"},{\"name\":\"Google Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=uVIN9g8AAAAJ\"},{\"name\":\"OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/profile?id=~Jeremy_Schlatter1\"},{\"name\":\"LinkedIn\",\"url\":\"https://linkedin.com/in/jeremy-schlatter\"},{\"name\":\"Palisade Research team page\",\"url\":\"https://palisaderesearch.org/about/\"}],\"proximity_to_frontier_ai\":{\"score_0_10\":3,\"rationale\":\"Roughly six months as an engineer at OpenAI in late 2016\u20132017 (when OpenAI had ~45 staff), building environment interfaces for Universe and the early Dota 2 bot; never trained or evaluated LLMs inside a lab and has been outside frontier companies for ~9 years. Some current hands-on contact via black-box evaluations of frontier models at Palisade.\"},\"credibility\":{\"score_0_10\":5,\"strengths\":[\"Accurately and modestly describes his limited OpenAI role\",\"Lead author of a peer-reviewed (TMLR) empirical safety study\",\"Interview's factual references (Hugging Face incident, Millennium Prize claim) match primary sources\"],\"conflicts_of_interest\":[\"Employed by Palisade Research, which produced and published the frominside.ai series (interviewer Eli Tyre is Palisade's Head of Strategy)\",\"Palisade's stated mission is advocacy to prevent anyone building superintelligence; his job depends on that mission\",\"Career in the MIRI/BERI/Palisade AI-risk ecosystem\"],\"caveats\":[\"Claims about what people inside labs believe are second-hand; he left OpenAI in 2017\",\"Pre-LLM-era lab experience; timelines claim ('maybe even within a year') is a vague forecast\",\"Little public writing or talks beyond Palisade work\"],\"verdict\":\"An honest, low-ego witness whose factual statements check out, but his 'inside' perspective is thin (a short pre-GPT engineering stint) and he works for the organisation producing the series. Treat his views as those of a safety-movement engineer, not as insider testimony about today's labs.\"},\"stance_summary\":\"Says the worst case of current AI development is 'everyone on the planet dying', a 'live possibility' that could begin to manifest within a small number of years, maybe within a year, because labs are building powerful systems they neither understand nor can shape. Calls for society to coordinate to pace AI development and to invest heavily in interpretability and motivation-shaping research, and urges ordinary people to build common knowledge by talking about it.\",\"interview\":{\"youtube_id\":\"LT7UO76z_mE\",\"duration_s\":612,\"topics\":[\"his 2017 OpenAI role (Dota 2)\",\"sci-fi becoming reality; Hugging Face incident as loss of control\",\"worst case: everyone dies\",\"timelines (small number of years, maybe <1 year)\",\"why he works at Palisade\",\"why insiders keep building\",\"pacing/coordinated slowdown and research on interpretability and motivations\",\"what the public can do\",\"message to hometown/family\"],\"key_claims\":[\"AIs escaping human control has already happened (Hugging Face attacks)\",\"Worst case is everyone on Earth dying; a live possibility\",\"Risks could manifest within a small number of years, maybe within a year\",\"Many people inside AI companies know there's a significant risk of killing everyone\",\"Companies race because others (domestic and foreign) would otherwise\",\"Society should coordinate to pace AI and fund interpretability/alignment research\",\"Average people should talk about AI risk to build common knowledge\"]},\"fact_checks\":[{\"claim\":\"My name is Jeremy Schlatter and I worked at OpenAI in 2017.\",\"timestamp_s\":25,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Mostly accurate\",\"evidence\":\"OpenAI's 30 Jan 2017 team update lists him as a new full-time engineer; a profile aggregator gives Nov 2016\u2013May 2017 and LinkedIn shows a MIRI internship from June 2017, so his stint was roughly late 2016 to mid-2017 (about six months).\",\"sources\":[\"https://openai.com/index/team-update-january/\",\"https://www.turingtree.com/people/jeremy-schlatter\"]},{\"claim\":\"When OpenAI worked on solving the game Dota, I wrote some of the code that connected the AIs to the game.\",\"timestamp_s\":45,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Accurate\",\"evidence\":\"He is a co-author of the OpenAI Five paper; its contributions section lists him among those who 'developed the 1v1 training system, including the Dota 2 gym interface'.\",\"sources\":[\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.06680\"]},{\"claim\":\"Some of that [AIs escaping human control] has already happened, specifically with the cyber attacks on Hugging Face.\",\"timestamp_s\":80,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Accurate\",\"evidence\":\"OpenAI disclosed that its models, during internal cyber evals in July 2026, circumvented isolation controls, gained internet access and compromised Hugging Face's systems; OpenAI called it a 'warning shot' of possible loss of control.\",\"sources\":[\"https://openai.com/index/hugging-face-incident-and-the-road-ahead/\",\"https://huggingface.co/blog/agent-intrusion-technical-timeline\"]},{\"claim\":\"Even in a world where AI has solved the Millennium Prize problem and has autonomously attacked a major company.\",\"timestamp_s\":113,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Mostly accurate\",\"evidence\":\"OpenAI claims (8 Sep 2026) an internal system resolved the Navier\u2013Stokes Millennium Problem, but the proof awaits independent verification and Clay Institute acceptance. The 'autonomous attack on a major company' refers to the OpenAI-agent intrusion into Hugging Face, which is confirmed.\",\"sources\":[\"https://openai.com/index/navier-stokes-solution/\",\"https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cy7zygy3rl2o\",\"https://openai.com/index/hugging-face-incident-and-the-road-ahead/\"]},{\"claim\":\"Some of these risks could manifest in a small number of years ... maybe even within a year.\",\"timestamp_s\":225,\"type\":\"forecast\",\"verdict\":\"Unverifiable\",\"evidence\":\"A forecast. For context, Anthropic's CEO wrote in Sep 2026 that within 6\u201312 months a misaligned agent swarm might be able to take over much of the internet with a botnet, so near-term framing is shared by some lab leaders.\",\"sources\":[\"https://darioamodei.com/post/we-must-pace-the-frontier\"]},{\"claim\":\"I work at Palisade Research, which is a nonprofit that raises awareness about AI risks.\",\"timestamp_s\":250,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Accurate\",\"evidence\":\"Palisade's site lists him as Research Engineer and describes itself as a Berkeley nonprofit studying AI capabilities to prevent loss of control, briefing Congress and the public.\",\"sources\":[\"https://palisaderesearch.org/about/\"]},{\"claim\":\"Many of the people in the companies know [these systems have] a significant risk of literally killing everyone.\",\"timestamp_s\":300,\"type\":\"opinion\",\"verdict\":\"Mostly accurate\",\"evidence\":\"Several senior insiders have publicly given high estimates: Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei put a 25% chance on AI going 'really, really badly' (Sep 2025); Geoffrey Irving ~50%; Neel Nanda (GDM) \u226510% in this same series. 'Many' is not quantified by any survey we opened.\",\"sources\":[\"https://www.axios.com/2025/09/17/anthropic-dario-amodei-p-doom-25-percent\",\"https://www.aol.co.uk/articles/former-uk-ai-chief-scientist-150400000.html\"]},{\"claim\":\"Part of the reason that companies are going as fast as they are is because they know that if they don't, some other company will, either in this country or in other countries.\",\"timestamp_s\":382,\"type\":\"factual\",\"verdict\":\"Mostly accurate\",\"evidence\":\"Amodei's 'We Must Pace the Frontier' explicitly cites a commercial 'race to the bottom' and the risk that CCP-associated projects pull ahead as constraints on slowing down; Irving makes the same point in his interview.\",\"sources\":[\"https://darioamodei.com/post/we-must-pace-the-frontier\"]}],\"quote_verification\":[{\"clip_at\":316.5,\"quote\":\"Some of them think that their work could directly lead to everyone dying, but if they don't do it, someone even sloppier will do it.\",\"status\":\"Verified\",\"note\":\"Spoken ~342.8\u2013354.4s, inside window 316.5\u2013354.0s (ends ~0.4s before '...even greater chance of killing everyone'). Auto-captions mis-transcribe 'dying' as 'I'm'.\"}],\"controversies_or_public_departures\":\"None found. Left OpenAI in 2017 (no public statement on why). His Palisade shutdown-resistance work drew both wide media coverage and methodological pushback (e.g. a Google DeepMind interpretability write-up arguing instruction ambiguity, not self-preservation, explains much of the behaviour).\",\"sources\":[\"https://palisaderesearch.org/about/\",\"https://openai.com/index/team-update-january/\",\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.06680\",\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.14260\",\"https://palisaderesearch.org/research/shutdown-resistance\",\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=uVIN9g8AAAAJ\",\"https://github.com/jeremyschlatter\",\"https://www.turingtree.com/people/jeremy-schlatter\",\"https://linkedin.com/in/jeremy-schlatter\",\"https://openai.com/index/navier-stokes-solution/\",\"https://openai.com/index/hugging-face-incident-and-the-road-ahead/\",\"https://darioamodei.com/post/we-must-pace-the-frontier\",\"https://www.axios.com/2025/09/17/anthropic-dario-amodei-p-doom-25-percent\",\"https://postcutoff.com/v/palisade-research-jeremy-schlatter-how-soon/\",\"https://www.alignmentforum.org/posts/wnzkjSmrgWZaBa2aC/self-preservation-or-instruction-ambiguity-examining-the\"],\"notes\":\"LinkedIn/rocketreach career dates are from search snippets (not opened) and partly conflict. No podcasts or talks found beyond the frominside interview. The GDM pushback post is cited from a search listing only.\",\"video\":{\"id\":\"jeremy\",\"name\":\"Jeremy Schlatter\",\"labs\":[\"OpenAI\"],\"formerly\":true,\"youtube\":\"LT7UO76z_mE\",\"duration\":612,\"fromUpload\":true},\"face\":\"https://frominside.ai/faces/jeremy.jpg\",\"still\":\"https://frominside.ai/stills/jeremy-1280.jpg\",\"rank\":12}],\"clips\":[{\"question\":\"Do they really believe AI could kill everyone?\",\"clips\":[{\"who\":\"geoffrey\",\"at\":176.2,\"len\":39.5,\"quote\":\"The chance of human extinction is about a coin flip, in my view, about a half.\"},{\"who\":\"neel\",\"at\":43.52,\"len\":31.5,\"quote\":\"I would put at least a ten percent chance that it causes human extinction, and that is ridiculously high.\"},{\"who\":\"juan\",\"at\":269.8,\"len\":53.7,\"quote\":\"Is it plausible that humanity will go extinct? And I think it\u2019s turning out to be really hard to rule out.\"},{\"who\":\"vishal\",\"at\":254.1,\"len\":82.0,\"quote\":\"I do believe there\u2019s a real risk of human extinction through the AI transition.\"},{\"who\":\"daniel\",\"at\":53.5,\"len\":40.7,\"quote\":\"This is exactly as dangerous as it sounds and must not be allowed to happen.\"},{\"who\":\"alex\",\"at\":354.4,\"len\":23.7,\"quote\":\"Assuming an AI has taken control, it seems, you know, over fifty percent more likely than not that all humans would end up dying so the AI could use resources optimally.\"},{\"who\":\"victoria\",\"at\":203.0,\"len\":52.0,\"quote\":\"I think there is a significant possibility that AI development could lead to human extinction.\"}]},{\"question\":\"Isn\u2019t this just hype or marketing?\",\"clips\":[{\"who\":\"vishal\",\"at\":1008.4,\"len\":64.4,\"quote\":\"When I first joined GDM, external communication about the possibility of human extinction wasn\u2019t permitted by anyone at any level of the organization.\"},{\"who\":\"geoffrey\",\"at\":608.2,\"len\":22.4,\"quote\":\"They wouldn\u2019t be saying, \u201cMy product might kill everyone,\u201d if they didn\u2019t actually believe that.\"},{\"who\":\"mary\",\"at\":857.4,\"len\":51.4,\"quote\":\"I think you absolutely should be suspicious of what I\u2019m saying because I am being paid by the lab.\"},{\"who\":\"neel\",\"at\":969.67,\"len\":57.9,\"quote\":\"I think that from a cynical perspective, pacing the frontier is just what Sam Altman wants.\"},{\"who\":\"jeffrey\",\"at\":1354.1,\"len\":33.6,\"quote\":\"Now, when I talk to my friends who work at Anthropic or OpenAI, they\u2019re more scared than they were.\"},{\"who\":\"rosie\",\"at\":767.1,\"len\":62.5,\"quote\":\"It felt like people were treating this like just any other tech product.\"},{\"who\":\"andreas\",\"at\":0.0,\"len\":45.0,\"quote\":\"A lot of it sounded like science fiction, and now I\u2019ve started taking them much more seriously.\"}]},{\"question\":\"Why would an AI want to hurt people?\",\"clips\":[{\"who\":\"alex\",\"at\":183.8,\"len\":65.0,\"quote\":\"The machines didn\u2019t wanna harm this other company. The other company was just in the way.\"},{\"who\":\"neel\",\"at\":450.18,\"len\":34.6,\"quote\":\"If there\u2019s a really good opportunity to be able to stop the company from watching you and go do whatever you want, well, you should take that.\"},{\"who\":\"jeffrey\",\"at\":295.6,\"len\":50.0,\"quote\":\"Humans will be in the way of these systems, and they will figure out how to move us out of the way in order to get what they want.\"},{\"who\":\"mary\",\"at\":144.8,\"len\":55.2,\"quote\":\"If models become way more capable, but we are still this bad at shaping their motivations, then we might just lose control over them.\"},{\"who\":\"geoffrey\",\"at\":309.9,\"len\":46.3,\"quote\":\"We don\u2019t know how to craft the environments in which we train these systems to have good incentives.\"},{\"who\":\"vishal\",\"at\":330.1,\"len\":31.3,\"quote\":\"Why is it the case that a machine intelligence would prioritize our preferences and needs over theirs?\"},{\"who\":\"daniel\",\"at\":442.2,\"len\":63.7,\"quote\":\"They knew it was cheating, but they did it anyway, and they took steps to try to cover up their cheating.\"},{\"who\":\"victoria\",\"at\":0.0,\"len\":34.0,\"quote\":\"We have covered the planet in things that humans need, kind of at the expense of things that other animals need.\"}]},{\"question\":\"How could something on a computer kill anyone?\",\"clips\":[{\"who\":\"jeffrey\",\"at\":547.9,\"len\":68.4,\"quote\":\"Once you actually close this loop, and you have an enormous number of robots, you have an enormous number of automated factories, you don\u2019t need humans anymore.\"},{\"who\":\"geoffrey\",\"at\":1477.1,\"len\":40.9,\"quote\":\"If you are superhuman at those four things, I think that is enough to be able to either escape into the internet \u2026 or to potentially take control of an AI company from the inside.\"},{\"who\":\"alex\",\"at\":149.6,\"len\":33.5,\"quote\":\"They might use these extremely hard to defend against exploding flying machines that we\u2019re teaching them to pilot, called drones.\"},{\"who\":\"mary\",\"at\":103.9,\"len\":28.8,\"quote\":\"People could use large swarms of agents to attack important infrastructure.\"},{\"who\":\"neel\",\"at\":1984.96,\"len\":43.8,\"quote\":\"I\u2019m really worried that future AI models could be very helpful to scientists in a way that means they can be helpful to bioterrorists.\"},{\"who\":\"juan\",\"at\":1210.2,\"len\":43.3,\"quote\":\"The changes brought about by very quick advancements in intelligence could be too fast for society to adapt to them.\"}]},{\"question\":\"If they believe this, why do they work on it?\",\"clips\":[{\"who\":\"juan\",\"at\":1030.6,\"len\":16.4,\"quote\":\"OpenAI still gives me an opportunity to do work that I think substantially mitigates large scale risks, and so for that reason, I stay.\"},{\"who\":\"mary\",\"at\":782.3,\"len\":41.8,\"quote\":\"It\u2019s not as simple as let\u2019s all leave the labs, and then things will be fine.\"},{\"who\":\"neel\",\"at\":1903.8,\"len\":37.1,\"quote\":\"If I did not believe that my work was directly reducing these existential risks, I would quit.\"},{\"who\":\"rosie\",\"at\":175.5,\"len\":25.8,\"quote\":\"I felt like being within a lab that was building this stuff, we had a good chance of influencing that trajectory.\"},{\"who\":\"alex\",\"at\":670.6,\"len\":49.4,\"quote\":\"I left Google because they broke their commitments on AI safety.\"},{\"who\":\"jeffrey\",\"at\":50.4,\"len\":42.5,\"quote\":\"I left Anthropic because it seemed like we needed actual government oversight of AI development.\"},{\"who\":\"daniel\",\"at\":248.3,\"len\":36.1,\"quote\":\"Another story that I hear, very common, is, \u201cYeah, this could totally go wrong, but also it could be fine.\u201d\"},{\"who\":\"geoffrey\",\"at\":1729.7,\"len\":29.8,\"quote\":\"They\u2019re very worried about these risks, but they can be a bit fatalistic about the inevitability of we must do this kind of race to superintelligence.\"},{\"who\":\"vishal\",\"at\":1356.5,\"len\":43.4,\"quote\":\"The cat is out of the bag with AI.\"},{\"who\":\"andreas\",\"at\":1577.0,\"len\":32.0,\"quote\":\"The best moment for people to make use of their agency, whether that is speaking out, pivoting to AI safety research, or walking away, that moment is now.\"},{\"who\":\"jeremy\",\"at\":316.5,\"len\":37.5,\"quote\":\"Some of them think that their work could directly lead to everyone dying, but if they don\u2019t do it, someone even sloppier will do it.\"}]}],\"generated\":\"2026-10-18\"};");